	(text "NIBBLE CARD PROG - PROGRAM MEMORY: four words of 8 bits on DIP switches, jumpered to their place in the 256-word space"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a9daf006-a505-48c1-bc35-fd40099f6829")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  41 transistors, 28 resistors, 5 LEDs, 4 DIP-8 switches, 32 diodes, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).  One design, one card per four words.\nFrom the bus: PC7..PC0.   To the bus: M7..M0 through diodes (the hub holds M low; the cards OR together).\nPC1..0 select the word.  PC7..2 are compared with the six jumpers: jumper k picks PC(k) (pins 2-3, '1') or its inverse (pins 1-2, '0'); the card holds addresses 4c..4c+3 where c = PC7..2.\nA row line goes high while its word is selected and the card matches; every closed switch on that row pulls its M line high through a diode.  Closed = 1.\nBit 7 (the top switch of each word) is the top bit of the opcode; bit 0 the low bit of the operand.  Blank memory (all open) reads 0000 0000 = NOP."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "23fbc4c1-f703-450b-aeb1-4cc1121bacfe")
	)
	(text "CARD SELECT: jumper k picks PC(k) or its inverse as JS(k), k = 7..2 (the page PC7..4 and the word group PC3..2 this card holds); SEL = all six JS high"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ad77a79a-cac3-4604-a110-3746e4d3eafe")
	)
